372
00:21:35,127 --> 00:21:36,294
‎From who, Do-mi?

373
00:21:36,295 --> 00:21:38,170
‎Was it Mr. Hong?
‎Did you tell him about me?

374
00:21:38,171 --> 00:21:39,714
‎No, I did not.

375
00:21:39,715 --> 00:21:40,924
‎I can't believe you guys!

376
00:21:45,178 --> 00:21:46,596
‎Who is it?

377
00:21:49,766 --> 00:21:51,350
‎Just a comment, please!

378
00:21:51,351 --> 00:21:52,852
‎Did you really copy that song?

379
00:21:52,853 --> 00:21:54,395
‎-Hyun-woo!
‎-Just a comment!

380
00:21:54,396 --> 00:21:57,023
‎-Aren't you going to release a statement?
‎-Just a moment!

381
00:21:57,024 --> 00:21:58,816
‎-Is it really true?
‎-Why did you...

382
00:21:58,817 --> 00:22:00,651
‎Hiding from us won't solve anything!

383
00:22:00,652 --> 00:22:02,571
‎Hyun-woo! Just one comment, please.

384
00:22:07,159 --> 00:22:08,618
‎What the hell is going on?

385
00:22:10,662 --> 00:22:12,873
‎Yes, this must be a dream.

386
00:22:13,457 --> 00:22:16,376
‎One blink,
‎and I'll wake up from this nightmare.

387
00:22:19,338 --> 00:22:21,923
‎PRESENT DAY

388
00:22:46,615 --> 00:22:50,744
<i>‎"I never wanted to embarrass myself
‎in front of my boyfriend."</i>

389
00:22:51,244 --> 00:22:53,662
<i>‎"But one day, a crisis struck."</i>

390
00:22:53,663 --> 00:22:56,917
‎"It was at our very first meeting
‎with his parents."

391
00:22:57,793 --> 00:22:58,834
‎"Guess what happened?"

392
00:22:58,835 --> 00:23:02,422
‎"I ended up sitting on his dad's lap!"

393
00:23:04,925 --> 00:23:07,343
‎HE THINKS IT'S FUNNY
‎CAN'T STAND HIS LAUGH

394
00:23:07,344 --> 00:23:08,929
‎WHO'S THIS GUY? JUST SOME DUDE?

395
00:23:15,894 --> 00:23:16,895
‎Hyun-woo.

396
00:23:21,108 --> 00:23:24,069
‎You know, I was a huge fan of Triangle.

397
00:23:28,448 --> 00:23:29,825
‎Yeah, I could tell.

398
00:23:30,742 --> 00:23:34,329
‎The way all four of you hit every move
‎in sync back then was so cool.

399
00:23:37,624 --> 00:23:38,500
‎There were three of us.

400
00:23:40,502 --> 00:23:41,586
‎Oh, three, right.

401
00:23:43,338 --> 00:23:45,507
‎You were the top trio boy group
‎in the game.

402
00:23:46,633 --> 00:23:47,467
‎We were a co-ed group.

403
00:23:52,931 --> 00:23:53,764
‎Bastard.

404
00:23:53,765 --> 00:23:54,974
‎What?

405
00:23:54,975 --> 00:23:55,891
‎I said "guest."

406
00:23:55,892 --> 00:23:58,395
‎I'm a permanent cast member,
‎and you're a bas...

407
00:23:59,813 --> 00:24:01,064
‎I mean, guest.

408
00:24:07,779 --> 00:24:08,697
‎"Guest."

409
00:24:10,323 --> 00:24:11,825
‎Thanks for everything.

410
00:24:14,077 --> 00:24:15,287
‎Is the lineup getting shuffled?

411
00:24:16,913 --> 00:24:19,915
‎-Is the show getting canceled?
‎-Oh, of course not.

412
00:24:19,916 --> 00:24:21,834
‎Not with the high ratings we're getting.

413
00:24:21,835 --> 00:24:24,629
‎So it's just me who's getting cut?

414
00:24:26,423 --> 00:24:28,716
‎Blame it on my incompetence.

415
00:24:28,717 --> 00:24:29,885
‎Mr. Oh.

416
00:24:30,802 --> 00:24:33,345
‎You know this is
‎the only show I do right now.

417
00:24:33,346 --> 00:24:34,847
‎You have another show on cable.

418
00:24:34,848 --> 00:24:37,434
‎I got cut from that show
‎over six months ago.

419
00:24:39,144 --> 00:24:42,189
‎We're not close enough
‎for me to know those things.

420
00:24:43,481 --> 00:24:46,192
‎We can just get closer from now on.

421
00:24:46,193 --> 00:24:47,444
‎We're the same age.

422
00:24:48,862 --> 00:24:49,820
‎I'm a year older.

423
00:24:49,821 --> 00:24:51,072
‎Bro, what's the reason?

424
00:24:52,574 --> 00:24:54,408
‎What did I do wrong, bro?

425
00:24:54,409 --> 00:24:58,078
‎You've been out of the scene for so long
‎that people don't know you enough.

426
00:24:58,079 --> 00:25:02,083
‎Comments have been blowing up, asking
‎why we keep bringing in a non-celebrity.

427
00:25:03,877 --> 00:25:05,795
‎Me? A non-celebrity?

428
00:25:06,379 --> 00:25:08,214
‎You should've
‎at least done a variety show.

429
00:25:08,215 --> 00:25:10,174
‎Megaton's Na Tae-poong
‎took off on variety,

430
00:25:10,175 --> 00:25:12,092
‎and now he's everywhere.

431
00:25:12,093 --> 00:25:13,929
‎He's even done several commercials.

432
00:25:16,014 --> 00:25:16,848
‎See you around then.

433
00:25:17,432 --> 00:25:18,266
‎But...

434
00:25:22,145 --> 00:25:22,979
‎Jeez.

435
00:25:24,105 --> 00:25:25,357
‎"Non-celebrity"?

436
00:25:26,566 --> 00:25:27,609
‎Me, a non-celebrity?

437
00:25:30,946 --> 00:25:32,572
‎Yes, non-celebrity speaking.

438
00:25:34,407 --> 00:25:36,451
‎This is he, non-celebrity Hwang Hyun-woo.

439
00:25:38,578 --> 00:25:39,412
‎Who?

440
00:25:41,623 --> 00:25:42,874
‎Producer Gong Ji-tae?

441
00:25:43,959 --> 00:25:44,918
‎Of course, I know!

442
00:25:46,336 --> 00:25:47,754
‎I'm a huge fan

443
00:25:48,880 --> 00:25:50,173
‎of his variety shows.

444
00:25:51,174 --> 00:25:52,091
<i>‎A concert</i>

445
00:25:52,092 --> 00:25:55,219
‎in support of
‎Gangwon's Expo hosting bid?

446
00:25:55,220 --> 00:25:57,429
‎It'll be broadcast live nationwide
‎in two weeks.

447
00:25:57,430 --> 00:25:59,975
‎A few teams have backed out,
‎so I called you.

448
00:26:01,434 --> 00:26:02,769
‎Oh, but...

449
00:26:03,937 --> 00:26:05,437
‎Can't I go solo?

450
00:26:05,438 --> 00:26:07,190
‎I perform solo at events these days.

451
00:26:07,941 --> 00:26:11,694
‎Mr. Gong wants the original members
‎perform the original song,

452
00:26:11,695 --> 00:26:13,780
‎without remix or rearrangement.

453
00:26:16,074 --> 00:26:18,118
‎Are you guys still on bad terms?

454
00:26:18,827 --> 00:26:19,785
‎Yeah.

455
00:26:19,786 --> 00:26:20,704
‎Sorry?

456
00:26:21,788 --> 00:26:24,206
‎I mean, no. It's just that...

457
00:26:24,207 --> 00:26:27,584
‎It's just too sudden to contact them
‎and ask if they can perform.

458
00:26:27,585 --> 00:26:30,921
‎We're planning a music variety show
‎with the groups from this concert.

459
00:26:30,922 --> 00:26:32,132
‎In the second half of the year.

460
00:26:33,216 --> 00:26:34,133
‎A variety show?

461
00:26:34,134 --> 00:26:36,052
‎This would be a good opportunity for you.

462
00:26:37,512 --> 00:26:39,222
‎We'll do it, all three of us.

463
00:26:41,683 --> 00:26:42,767
‎Darn it.

464
00:26:45,186 --> 00:26:46,021
‎Hyun-woo.

465
00:26:48,189 --> 00:26:49,149
‎Hwang Hyun-woo.

466
00:26:50,442 --> 00:26:51,818
‎Man, this is wild!

467
00:26:52,485 --> 00:26:53,653
‎How have you been?

468
00:26:54,446 --> 00:26:56,865
‎-Hey.
‎-How have you been, man?

469
00:26:58,700 --> 00:26:59,951
‎Do I know you?

470
00:27:02,454 --> 00:27:03,913
‎It's me, Megaton's Na Tae-poong.

471
00:27:04,664 --> 00:27:05,998
‎I recognized you right away.

472
00:27:05,999 --> 00:27:10,294
‎-Come on, I'm on everything these days.
‎-Oh, Jang...

473
00:27:10,295 --> 00:27:11,963
‎I mean, Tae-poong.

474
00:27:12,547 --> 00:27:14,631
‎Hey, it's been so long.

475
00:27:14,632 --> 00:27:17,552
‎-I know. I guess you've been...
‎-Yeah.

476
00:27:19,637 --> 00:27:20,722
‎taking a break from shows.

477
00:27:25,602 --> 00:27:28,771
‎I'm a singer, after all.
‎I got an offer to perform at a concert.

478
00:27:28,772 --> 00:27:30,230
‎You know Gong Ji-tae, right?

479
00:27:30,231 --> 00:27:31,648
‎He's directing it.

480
00:27:31,649 --> 00:27:34,485
‎So you're doing the show
‎that I turned down?

481
00:27:34,486 --> 00:27:36,570
‎That's great, seriously.

482
00:27:36,571 --> 00:27:38,655
‎My schedule's been packed lately.

483
00:27:38,656 --> 00:27:40,909
‎I'm so exhausted
‎from all the events and shows.

484
00:27:41,409 --> 00:27:42,702
‎Seriously, it's just so...

485
00:27:43,828 --> 00:27:46,748
‎Hey, what's the next thing on my schedule?

486
00:27:47,540 --> 00:27:48,583
‎You're going home.

487
00:27:51,544 --> 00:27:53,754
‎Yeah, I finally get to take a break.

488
00:27:53,755 --> 00:27:54,672
‎-Oh, man.
‎-Right.

489
00:27:56,299 --> 00:27:57,591
‎All right then.

490
00:27:57,592 --> 00:27:59,093
‎-Take it easy.
‎-Yeah.

491
00:27:59,094 --> 00:28:00,136
‎-See you.
‎-Bye.

492
00:28:39,634 --> 00:28:41,219
‎MEGATON BAR

493
00:28:42,137 --> 00:28:44,514
‎He was practically invisible back then.

494
00:28:46,015 --> 00:28:48,726
‎I really had no idea
‎we'd take number one

495
00:28:48,727 --> 00:28:50,687
‎with the first song I ever wrote.

496
00:28:51,271 --> 00:28:54,398
<i>‎We love you all, our RGB Army!</i>

497
00:28:54,399 --> 00:28:56,608
‎Lung cancer, 100 million won.

498
00:28:56,609 --> 00:28:58,110
‎Liver cancer, another 100 million.

499
00:28:58,111 --> 00:28:59,903
‎Most cancer riders

500
00:28:59,904 --> 00:29:03,198
‎separate major and minor cancers,
‎but we do not.

501
00:29:03,199 --> 00:29:04,950
‎We don't make that distinction at all.

502
00:29:04,951 --> 00:29:08,663
‎So no matter the type of cancer,
‎once you're diagnosed,

503
00:29:10,915 --> 00:29:13,126
‎your life hits the jackpot
‎from that moment on.

504
00:29:14,461 --> 00:29:15,711
‎Oh, I'm sorry.

505
00:29:15,712 --> 00:29:17,838
‎It's not a jackpot if you get sick.

506
00:29:17,839 --> 00:29:18,840
‎Sorry, one moment.

507
00:29:21,676 --> 00:29:22,593
‎Sorry about that.

508
00:29:22,594 --> 00:29:25,180
‎-What I meant is...
‎-I need to use the restroom.

509
00:29:25,764 --> 00:29:28,141
‎Yes, of course. Please, go ahead.

510
00:29:30,477 --> 00:29:32,520
‎Man, who's calling?

511
00:29:36,441 --> 00:29:37,776
‎Yes, Gu Sang-gu speaking.

512
00:29:39,402 --> 00:29:40,820
‎What the hell? This bastard...

513
00:29:41,946 --> 00:29:42,864
‎Why's he... Huh?

514
00:29:44,282 --> 00:29:45,617
‎Stop calling, you bastard.

515
00:29:47,660 --> 00:29:50,120
‎Does this prick
‎still think he's the leader?

516
00:29:50,121 --> 00:29:51,498
‎Asshole.

517
00:29:54,250 --> 00:29:56,460
‎Why'd this jerk
‎suddenly go to the restroom?

518
00:29:56,461 --> 00:29:57,420
‎Is he taking a dump?

519
00:29:58,922 --> 00:30:02,467
‎It's always those idiots
‎who have to poop when they're out...

520
00:30:18,233 --> 00:30:20,108
<i>‎Read it forward, it's Gu Sang-gu</i>

521
00:30:20,109 --> 00:30:21,611
<i>‎Read it backward, still Gu Sang-gu</i>

522
00:30:22,529 --> 00:30:24,072
<i>‎Gu Sang-gu, the unstoppable rapper</i>

523
00:30:24,948 --> 00:30:25,949
‎You crazy little...

524
00:30:27,659 --> 00:30:29,452
‎You really came all the way to my place.

525
00:30:31,287 --> 00:30:33,747
‎You said to come meet you at your place.

526
00:30:33,748 --> 00:30:36,124
‎Yeah, only if you had a death wish.

527
00:30:36,125 --> 00:30:38,544
‎See? You did tell me to come over.

528
00:30:38,545 --> 00:30:40,588
‎Sang-gu, my man. Let's do it.

529
00:30:41,464 --> 00:30:44,425
‎A concert in support of
‎Gangwon's Expo hosting bid!

530
00:30:45,802 --> 00:30:47,719
‎Shut up and get lost.

531
00:30:47,720 --> 00:30:50,681
‎Come on, you really were
‎the best rapper out there.

532
00:30:50,682 --> 00:30:52,475
‎Let's take the stage again.

533
00:30:53,226 --> 00:30:55,895
‎Don't you remember
‎what you said to me back then?

534
00:30:57,438 --> 00:30:59,189
‎You left me to take the fall

535
00:30:59,190 --> 00:31:01,276
‎for that plagiarism scandal alone,
‎and now what?

536
00:31:01,901 --> 00:31:03,278
‎You're selling me insurance?

537
00:31:04,737 --> 00:31:06,780
‎Wait! I'm sorry.

538
00:31:06,781 --> 00:31:08,949
‎Hyun-woo, I'm starving.

539
00:31:08,950 --> 00:31:11,827
‎My stomach keeps growling at me.

540
00:31:11,828 --> 00:31:14,371
‎It won't stop talking to me. "Growl!"

541
00:31:14,372 --> 00:31:17,165
‎"Growl!" My stomach won't stop growling.

542
00:31:17,166 --> 00:31:18,293
‎Get lost.

543
00:31:19,794 --> 00:31:21,461
‎Don't ever show up in front of me again.

544
00:31:21,462 --> 00:31:23,631
‎You said never to show up
‎in front of you again!

545
00:31:24,215 --> 00:31:25,424
‎Come on!

546
00:31:25,425 --> 00:31:28,344
‎That's why I showed up in front of you.

547
00:31:28,845 --> 00:31:29,679
‎Sang-gu.

548
00:31:30,263 --> 00:31:33,892
‎We've both hurt each other once,
‎so let's put it behind us now, okay?

549
00:31:34,392 --> 00:31:35,310
‎Let's get back together.

550
00:31:36,060 --> 00:31:37,061
‎Triangle!

551
00:31:41,274 --> 00:31:42,692
‎What... Hey!

552
00:31:56,372 --> 00:31:57,373
‎Long time no see, Sang-gu.

553
00:31:57,957 --> 00:31:59,207
‎I almost forgot your face.

554
00:31:59,208 --> 00:32:02,670
‎Mr. Ko, I'm really sorry.
‎I should've been in touch.

555
00:32:04,797 --> 00:32:06,298
‎Who's he? A tagalong?

556
00:32:06,299 --> 00:32:08,134
‎He was with him, so we brought him along.

557
00:32:11,721 --> 00:32:12,764
‎Are you two close?

558
00:32:17,435 --> 00:32:18,268
‎Well,

559
00:32:18,269 --> 00:32:20,896
‎we're close enough
‎that he'd gladly take up the offer

560
00:32:20,897 --> 00:32:24,317
‎if I asked him to perform with me
‎at the Gangwon Expo concert.

561
00:32:25,068 --> 00:32:26,778
‎-We're about that close.
‎-So...

562
00:32:30,740 --> 00:32:32,075
‎you're close enough

563
00:32:34,077 --> 00:32:36,162
‎to share some real pain, right?

564
00:32:37,038 --> 00:32:38,957
‎No, not quite. Take care, sir.

565
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:42,751
‎-Sang-gu.
‎-Yes?

566
00:32:42,752 --> 00:32:44,294
‎When are you paying me back?

567
00:32:44,295 --> 00:32:46,296
‎How much can you make
‎selling insurance anyway?

568
00:32:46,297 --> 00:32:49,424
‎Mr. Ko, I'm selling insurance
‎to rebuild my credit.

569
00:32:49,425 --> 00:32:52,552
‎Once my credit's back, I'll get a loan
‎and pay you back in one shot.

570
00:32:52,553 --> 00:32:53,595
‎I promise!

571
00:32:53,596 --> 00:32:54,514
‎Do you...

572
00:32:56,015 --> 00:32:57,182
‎really have a death wish?

573
00:32:57,183 --> 00:32:58,851
‎No, I do not!

574
00:32:59,769 --> 00:33:00,853
‎Please don't kill my friend.

575
00:33:03,398 --> 00:33:05,274
‎-How much does he owe you?
‎-300 million.

576
00:33:06,693 --> 00:33:08,611
‎-I see.
‎-Hey, wait!

577
00:33:09,862 --> 00:33:11,738
‎Help me. They might really kill me.

578
00:33:11,739 --> 00:33:13,573
‎You crazy bastard. Seriously, 300 million?

579
00:33:13,574 --> 00:33:15,742
‎What's the Gangwon Concert about?

580
00:33:15,743 --> 00:33:17,328
‎Will that make me money?

581
00:33:21,332 --> 00:33:24,001
‎The producer is pretty famous.

582
00:33:24,002 --> 00:33:27,421
‎If we do well,
‎we'll get a regular spot on his show,

583
00:33:27,422 --> 00:33:30,800
‎perform at events, land commercials,
‎and make a lot of money.

584
00:33:31,384 --> 00:33:34,303
‎Didn't Megaton's Na Tae-poong blow up
‎through variety shows too?

585
00:33:36,597 --> 00:33:37,515
‎What does he do?

586
00:33:38,099 --> 00:33:40,183
‎He produced my solo album.

587
00:33:40,184 --> 00:33:41,769
‎That's not the only thing I funded.

588
00:34:01,247 --> 00:34:02,123
‎You two.

589
00:34:03,041 --> 00:34:04,292
‎Can you make a comeback?

590
00:34:08,963 --> 00:34:09,881
‎Us two?

591
00:34:12,508 --> 00:34:15,136
‎From now on,
‎you two will work hard to pay me back.

592
00:34:16,304 --> 00:34:17,513
‎You got that?

593
00:34:18,014 --> 00:34:18,848
‎Why should I?

594
00:34:23,561 --> 00:34:24,561
‎Pay me back.

595
00:34:24,562 --> 00:34:26,773
‎I'll do my very best, sir.

596
00:34:29,567 --> 00:34:30,943
‎It hurts so much.

597
00:34:35,948 --> 00:34:37,450
‎-Goodbye.
‎-Thank you.

598
00:34:40,536 --> 00:34:43,413
‎Who do you think you are
‎to release a solo album?

599
00:34:43,414 --> 00:34:45,957
‎I barely had any rap lines
‎in Triangle songs.

600
00:34:45,958 --> 00:34:48,210
‎Do-mi the singer, you the dancer,
‎and me, the filler.

601
00:34:48,211 --> 00:34:51,172
‎My psychiatrist said
‎I have a second-place complex.

602
00:34:52,006 --> 00:34:53,174
‎You're the third in the group.

603
00:34:54,425 --> 00:34:55,842
‎-Oh, the third...
‎-You saw a psychiatrist

604
00:34:55,843 --> 00:34:57,385
‎over not getting many rap lines?

605
00:34:57,386 --> 00:35:00,640
‎Don't you run your mouth about my rap.
‎Rap is my everything!

606
00:35:03,017 --> 00:35:05,269
‎Fine, we'll give you more rap lines.
‎Happy now?

607
00:35:07,230 --> 00:35:11,067
‎Then let me fill the intro,
‎instrumental break, and outro with my rap.

608
00:35:11,818 --> 00:35:14,069
‎We'll fill every empty spot with your rap.

609
00:35:14,070 --> 00:35:15,029
‎Really?

610
00:35:20,076 --> 00:35:22,078
‎Oh, wow.

611
00:35:24,831 --> 00:35:26,457
‎But hey, do you think Do-mi will do it?

612
00:35:27,333 --> 00:35:30,169
‎She married some
‎construction company owner, right?

613
00:35:30,670 --> 00:35:32,546
‎That's strange. Why didn't she invite me?

614
00:35:32,547 --> 00:35:33,965
‎I couldn't go either.

615
00:35:34,549 --> 00:35:36,717
‎-Really?
‎-Yeah, I was in jail.

616
00:35:40,096 --> 00:35:41,721
‎I knew you'd end up doing drugs.

617
00:35:41,722 --> 00:35:44,767
‎Not for drugs but for gambling.
‎Drugs are serious.

618
00:36:03,828 --> 00:36:04,661
‎Do-mi!

619
00:36:04,662 --> 00:36:06,371
‎Do-mi, it's you! Byeon Do-mi!

620
00:36:06,372 --> 00:36:08,665
‎It's you, right?
‎It's me, Hwang Hyun-woo!

621
00:36:08,666 --> 00:36:10,667
‎Hey, why did you ignore my calls?

622
00:36:10,668 --> 00:36:13,211
‎Let go of me. She knows me.

623
00:36:13,212 --> 00:36:15,256
‎Hey, Do-mi, Do-mi!

624
00:36:18,426 --> 00:36:19,802
‎See? She knows me.

625
00:36:21,053 --> 00:36:23,014
‎I don't know him. Take him away.

626
00:36:26,851 --> 00:36:27,727
‎Hey, Do-mi!

627
00:36:29,353 --> 00:36:30,229
‎Hey!

628
00:36:35,234 --> 00:36:42,074
‎HWANG HYUN-WOO:
‎LET'S GET BACK TOGETHER FOR A CONCERT!

629
00:36:46,579 --> 00:36:48,914
‎So you tried to blackmail me? How cute.

630
00:36:48,915 --> 00:36:50,540
‎Blackmail? No way.

631
00:36:50,541 --> 00:36:53,376
‎It's just a beautiful memory we share.

632
00:36:53,377 --> 00:36:55,254
‎How did you get my address?

633
00:36:56,172 --> 00:36:57,006
‎Through AI.

634
00:36:57,798 --> 00:36:59,507
‎AI told you my address?

635
00:36:59,508 --> 00:37:01,427
‎I upgraded to the paid version.

636
00:37:03,012 --> 00:37:05,430
‎I guess money really does
‎solve all problems.

637
00:37:05,431 --> 00:37:06,641
‎It'll be broadcast nationwide.

638
00:37:08,100 --> 00:37:10,436
‎We just have to perform our debut song,
‎and that's it.

639
00:37:11,020 --> 00:37:12,812
‎But why do we have to do it?

640
00:37:12,813 --> 00:37:14,981
‎We'll relive our dreams and memories--

641
00:37:14,982 --> 00:37:16,650
‎Cut the bullshit.

642
00:37:16,651 --> 00:37:18,194
‎Like we have any fond memories.

643
00:37:18,778 --> 00:37:19,695
‎You're right.

644
00:37:20,655 --> 00:37:22,240
‎You're always right.

645
00:37:23,658 --> 00:37:24,991
‎Help me out just this once.

646
00:37:24,992 --> 00:37:26,202
‎I'll be honest.

647
00:37:29,455 --> 00:37:30,790
‎This is my last chance.

648
00:37:32,458 --> 00:37:33,584
‎Please, help me.

649
00:37:35,419 --> 00:37:37,754
‎-Ms. Byeon Do-mi, please.
‎-Do you need money?

650
00:37:37,755 --> 00:37:39,173
‎Yes. What?

651
00:37:46,472 --> 00:37:49,474
‎There's no limit on this.
‎You can spend it all you want.

652
00:37:49,475 --> 00:37:50,559
‎Want it?

653
00:37:59,402 --> 00:38:00,403
‎Fine.

654
00:38:02,655 --> 00:38:05,324
‎Money is important,
‎and I need to make money.

655
00:38:05,950 --> 00:38:07,618
‎But money isn't everything.

656
00:38:08,494 --> 00:38:11,038
‎It's my dream. Think of our RGB Army.

657
00:38:13,249 --> 00:38:14,292
‎I'm serious.

658
00:38:16,043 --> 00:38:18,546
‎Can't you hear it?
‎My heart's pounding with excitement.

659
00:38:32,226 --> 00:38:33,978
‎I feel like my heart's about to burst.

660
00:38:39,025 --> 00:38:41,068
‎-Wait.
‎-Goddammit, don't follow me.

661
00:38:42,236 --> 00:38:44,363
‎If you do, I'll slap you.

662
00:38:51,746 --> 00:38:52,705
‎Hey!

663
00:38:54,707 --> 00:38:57,168
‎Be honest.
‎Don't you want to be on stage again too?

664
00:38:58,919 --> 00:39:00,421
‎Isn't that why you came here?

665
00:39:01,630 --> 00:39:05,009
‎The feeling when people went wild
‎for our dance and songs!

666
00:39:05,760 --> 00:39:06,677
‎That thrill.

667
00:39:08,512 --> 00:39:10,181
‎Let's get on stage just one more time.

668
00:39:10,848 --> 00:39:11,932
‎Come on, Do-mi.

669
00:39:13,309 --> 00:39:14,352
‎Bullshit.

670
00:39:22,068 --> 00:39:22,985
‎Right.

671
00:39:23,611 --> 00:39:25,529
‎Why would she?
‎She's married to a rich guy.

672
00:39:27,615 --> 00:39:30,825
‎I'm not very happy with
‎Jun-hoo's new English kindergarten,

673
00:39:30,826 --> 00:39:32,702
‎so he can stop going after this week.

674
00:39:32,703 --> 00:39:34,079
‎And starting next week,

675
00:39:34,080 --> 00:39:36,665
‎get him ready
‎for the advanced art classes.

676
00:39:39,460 --> 00:39:41,170
‎If you heard me, you should answer.

677
00:39:42,463 --> 00:39:43,714
‎You have no manners at all.

678
00:39:45,925 --> 00:39:47,426
‎I'm sorry, Mother. I...

679
00:39:48,928 --> 00:39:50,554
‎I have food in my mouth right now.

680
00:39:51,180 --> 00:39:52,973
‎I'll do as you said, Mother.

681
00:40:01,107 --> 00:40:02,066
<i>‎What the...</i>

682
00:40:05,986 --> 00:40:07,696
<i>‎Turn your head when you sneeze.</i>

683
00:40:08,614 --> 00:40:09,824
<i>‎You have no manners.</i>

684
00:40:11,409 --> 00:40:12,826
‎Gosh, I'm sorry, Mother.

685
00:40:12,827 --> 00:40:14,370
<i>‎You drive me crazy.</i>

686
00:40:14,912 --> 00:40:16,079
<i>‎Mr. Kang.</i>

687
00:40:16,080 --> 00:40:18,541
<i>‎Is the tree in the yard
‎being taken care of properly?</i>

688
00:40:19,041 --> 00:40:21,710
‎The new gardener is quite skilled, ma'am.

689
00:40:22,294 --> 00:40:25,381
<i>‎Great, show me. Move me to the garden.</i>

690
00:40:27,425 --> 00:40:29,635
‎Jeez, that is not normal.

691
00:40:30,970 --> 00:40:32,138
‎Is it only funny to me?

692
00:40:33,431 --> 00:40:35,974
<i>‎It's not time yet, I mean right now</i>

693
00:40:35,975 --> 00:40:38,017
<i>‎You shouldn't do that
‎You shouldn't do this</i>

694
00:40:38,018 --> 00:40:41,229
<i>‎-Why is it so complicated, baby
‎-Why is it so complicated, baby</i>

695
00:40:41,230 --> 00:40:45,316
<i>‎Love is, why is it, why is it
‎So hard?</i>

696
00:40:45,317 --> 00:40:50,780
<i>‎Even though every day, every day
‎You still make me laugh and cry</i>

697
00:40:50,781 --> 00:40:53,616
