925
00:54:34,312 --> 00:54:35,312
<i>‎It was him.</i>

926
00:54:35,313 --> 00:54:37,148
‎That bastard was Mr. Park.

927
00:54:37,983 --> 00:54:40,567
‎Okay, let's say he's Mr. Park.
‎But what can we do now?

928
00:54:40,568 --> 00:54:43,195
‎We need to take bloody revenge.

929
00:54:43,196 --> 00:54:44,948
‎Whose fault is it
‎that I ended up like this?

930
00:54:46,658 --> 00:54:49,869
‎Hey, I think I see his car.

931
00:54:53,790 --> 00:54:54,791
‎Shit.

932
00:54:55,834 --> 00:54:56,876
‎Bro, what are you doing?

933
00:54:57,919 --> 00:54:59,003
<i>‎We need to catch him!</i>

934
00:54:59,004 --> 00:55:01,755
<i>‎-What? No, don't do it.
‎-Step on it, or we'll lose him.</i>

935
00:55:01,756 --> 00:55:03,298
<i>‎I want my money. Step on it.</i>

936
00:55:03,299 --> 00:55:05,050
<i>‎-No, don't. Are you crazy?
‎-Go faster.</i>

937
00:55:05,051 --> 00:55:07,970
‎-What's with you, Do-mi?
‎-Let's go, hit the gas.

938
00:55:07,971 --> 00:55:10,431
‎-No, don't do it.
‎-Faster. Get closer.

939
00:55:10,432 --> 00:55:12,225
‎-Floor it!
‎-You're so dead.

940
00:55:19,024 --> 00:55:20,441
‎We got him.

941
00:55:20,442 --> 00:55:22,234
<i>‎-Go faster!
‎-No, stop!</i>

942
00:55:22,235 --> 00:55:23,778
‎Slow down, stop!

943
00:55:24,738 --> 00:55:26,156
‎Seriously, stop!

944
00:55:32,871 --> 00:55:33,830
‎Got you.

945
00:55:34,456 --> 00:55:36,415
‎-We got him, right here.
‎-You'll hit his car.

946
00:55:36,416 --> 00:55:38,792
‎-No, we're too close. You'll hit him.
‎-Hey!

947
00:55:38,793 --> 00:55:41,336
‎What if we crash into him?
‎We have to perform! Snap out of it!

948
00:55:41,337 --> 00:55:42,463
‎I know who you are!

949
00:55:42,464 --> 00:55:44,089
‎Hey, Park Yong-gu!

950
00:55:44,090 --> 00:55:45,924
<i>‎I want my money! Pay us what we're owed!</i>

951
00:55:45,925 --> 00:55:47,551
‎-Oh, no.
‎-Just ram him!

952
00:55:47,552 --> 00:55:49,219
‎-Have you lost your mind?
‎-Let's do it!

953
00:55:49,220 --> 00:55:50,679
‎-Are you crazy? Shut up!
‎-Ram him.

954
00:55:50,680 --> 00:55:52,097
‎Should I really do it?

955
00:55:52,098 --> 00:55:54,183
‎-Ram him. Do it.
‎-No, don't do it!

956
00:55:54,184 --> 00:55:56,185
‎-Do it.
‎-I'm doing it.

957
00:55:56,186 --> 00:55:57,144
‎Don't lose your head!

958
00:55:57,145 --> 00:55:58,437
‎-No!
‎-Just ram him!

959
00:55:58,438 --> 00:55:59,564
‎-Now!
‎-No!

960
00:56:14,704 --> 00:56:16,456
‎I told you not to do it.

961
00:56:17,415 --> 00:56:19,834
‎Hyun-woo, I think you're totally screwed.

962
00:56:20,502 --> 00:56:21,544
‎Oh, no.

963
00:56:27,300 --> 00:56:28,425
‎What do we do?

964
00:56:28,426 --> 00:56:30,427
‎-No.
‎-What do we do now?

965
00:56:30,428 --> 00:56:32,179
‎No!

966
00:56:32,180 --> 00:56:33,181
‎Hey!

967
00:56:34,432 --> 00:56:36,351
‎-Wait!
‎-Hey, wait up!

968
00:56:48,863 --> 00:56:50,406
‎Hey, Park Yong-gu?

969
00:56:53,493 --> 00:56:55,036
‎He's alive. He's breathing.

970
00:56:55,537 --> 00:56:56,370
‎-He's alive.
‎-He is?

971
00:56:56,371 --> 00:56:58,665
‎-Should we call the ambulance?
‎-Of course we should!

972
00:56:59,582 --> 00:57:00,499
‎Why are you asking me?

973
00:57:00,500 --> 00:57:02,501
‎You got all worked up
‎and nearly killed him.

974
00:57:02,502 --> 00:57:05,964
‎So you'd be getting arrested, not me,
‎which is why I'm asking you.

975
00:57:06,548 --> 00:57:08,049
‎-I'd get arrested?
‎-Yeah.

976
00:57:09,092 --> 00:57:10,509
‎Do-mi, you egged me on!

977
00:57:10,510 --> 00:57:12,386
‎-Right.
‎-Oh! Hold on.

978
00:57:12,387 --> 00:57:14,681
‎-I think he just looked at me.
‎-Huh?

979
00:57:18,393 --> 00:57:19,309
‎What the hell?

980
00:57:19,310 --> 00:57:20,936
‎Are you sure you weren't mistaken?

981
00:57:20,937 --> 00:57:22,438
‎-Should I just slap him?
‎-Don't!

982
00:57:22,439 --> 00:57:24,774
‎What if he's really hurt
‎and you make it worse?

983
00:57:25,358 --> 00:57:26,483
‎Let's get him into the car first.

984
00:57:26,484 --> 00:57:28,068
‎We'll either take him to a hospital or...

985
00:57:28,069 --> 00:57:30,237
‎-Or bury him in the woods.
‎-Yes, in the woods...

986
00:57:30,238 --> 00:57:32,157
‎Hey! That never even crossed my mind.

987
00:57:35,368 --> 00:57:36,536
‎-My gosh.
‎-Man, he's heavy.

988
00:57:40,248 --> 00:57:42,500
‎-Oh, no.
‎-You can't lose your grip!

989
00:57:43,084 --> 00:57:45,211
‎-No!
‎-I had a tight grip on him!

990
00:57:48,256 --> 00:57:49,466
‎-What do we do?
‎-Shit.

991
00:57:50,008 --> 00:57:51,885
‎-Gosh, what do we do?
‎-Pick him up!

992
00:57:56,639 --> 00:57:59,851
‎-Damn it, not again!
‎-Why do you keep losing your grip?

993
00:58:02,979 --> 00:58:04,063
‎I'm not doing this.

994
00:58:11,154 --> 00:58:12,572
‎-Oh, man.
‎-Was I mistaken?

995
00:58:13,448 --> 00:58:14,699
‎He hasn't opened his eyes once.

996
00:58:16,868 --> 00:58:19,453
‎What if he's actually dead now
‎because you kept losing your grip?

997
00:58:19,454 --> 00:58:21,539
‎I was holding on tight.

998
00:58:29,547 --> 00:58:31,507
‎I'm sorry! I'm a novice driver.

999
00:58:31,508 --> 00:58:32,799
‎A novice?

1000
00:58:32,800 --> 00:58:34,677
‎And you're driving a dump truck?

1001
00:58:35,470 --> 00:58:38,305
‎Mister, watch where you're driving!

1002
00:58:38,306 --> 00:58:39,641
‎Are you okay? Are you hurt?

1003
00:58:40,975 --> 00:58:43,018
‎Did I kill anyone?
‎Please tell me I didn't.

1004
00:58:43,019 --> 00:58:46,231
‎-No, you didn't kill or hurt anyone here.
‎-Hide him.

1005
00:58:48,024 --> 00:58:49,567
‎Damn it.

1006
00:58:58,326 --> 00:59:00,953
‎Let me call the police first.

1007
00:59:00,954 --> 00:59:02,204
‎I'll turn myself in.

1008
00:59:02,205 --> 00:59:03,915
‎Put that phone down, right now!

1009
00:59:05,667 --> 00:59:06,542
‎What are you doing?

1010
00:59:06,543 --> 00:59:08,085
‎Put that down, now!

1011
00:59:08,086 --> 00:59:09,587
‎You're bleeding.

1012
00:59:10,171 --> 00:59:12,257
‎Sir, please let me call
‎my insurance company.

1013
00:59:13,841 --> 00:59:17,345
‎Driving can leave you a little hurt
‎or bleeding sometimes.

1014
00:59:21,099 --> 00:59:22,641
‎But the car's smashed in.

1015
00:59:22,642 --> 00:59:24,601
‎I said it's fine.
‎You're being really annoying.

1016
00:59:24,602 --> 00:59:25,603
‎Just go, please.

1017
00:59:29,524 --> 00:59:30,733
‎Hang on a second.

1018
00:59:31,442 --> 00:59:32,360
‎You people...

1019
00:59:37,156 --> 00:59:38,950
‎I know that lady.

1020
00:59:42,328 --> 00:59:43,162
‎Byeon...

1021
00:59:44,205 --> 00:59:45,039
‎Dom?

1022
00:59:46,833 --> 00:59:47,959
‎Rockfish?

1023
00:59:48,501 --> 00:59:51,003
‎How could someone's name be Rockfish?

1024
00:59:51,004 --> 00:59:54,006
‎Byeon Do-mi from Tambourine,
‎one of the top co-ed groups in the 2000s.

1025
00:59:54,007 --> 00:59:55,091
‎Right?

1026
00:59:56,968 --> 00:59:59,094
‎-Xylophone?
‎-We're Triangle.

1027
00:59:59,095 --> 01:00:00,138
‎Triangle!

1028
01:00:07,020 --> 01:00:08,270
‎All right.

1029
01:00:08,271 --> 01:00:10,356
‎I'm going to post about this online.

1030
01:00:11,149 --> 01:00:13,776
‎-Post what?
‎-About the generosity you showed me.

1031
01:00:15,737 --> 01:00:16,738
‎Yes, great idea!

1032
01:00:17,322 --> 01:00:19,740
‎-Go post it right now.
‎-Okay.

1033
01:00:19,741 --> 01:00:21,284
‎Go on, then.

1034
01:00:35,798 --> 01:00:37,925
‎Just go. It's fine.

1035
01:00:39,177 --> 01:00:40,345
‎I'm counting on that post!

1036
01:00:52,774 --> 01:00:55,817
‎Guys, we can get this all sorted out.
‎Just stay focused.

1037
01:00:55,818 --> 01:00:58,029
‎He'll post good stuff about us.
‎We just have to perform well.

1038
01:00:59,906 --> 01:01:00,907
‎Where did that man go?

1039
01:01:03,951 --> 01:01:04,785
‎Shit.

1040
01:01:04,786 --> 01:01:06,912
‎-Oh, what the...
‎-What happened?

1041
01:01:06,913 --> 01:01:08,289
‎So he wasn't dead after all.

1042
01:01:11,459 --> 01:01:12,460
‎There he is!

1043
01:01:14,837 --> 01:01:16,296
‎Park Yong-gu!

1044
01:01:16,297 --> 01:01:17,548
‎Stop right there!

1045
01:01:18,883 --> 01:01:21,010
‎I don't know you!

1046
01:01:29,686 --> 01:01:32,313
‎GANGWON 100KM

1047
01:01:47,870 --> 01:01:49,330
‎That's a size I don't see often.

1048
01:01:55,753 --> 01:01:57,213
‎URGENT WILDLIFE CONTROL TARGET

1049
01:02:00,800 --> 01:02:01,676
‎No.

1050
01:02:04,178 --> 01:02:05,888
‎I'm a singer, not a hunter.

1051
01:02:07,598 --> 01:02:08,599
‎Get it together.

1052
01:02:10,226 --> 01:02:12,311
<i>‎I like you</i>

1053
01:02:13,855 --> 01:02:15,565
<i>‎I like you</i>

1054
01:02:18,860 --> 01:02:21,696
<i>‎I like you</i>

1055
01:02:23,990 --> 01:02:25,783
<i>‎I like you</i>

1056
01:02:29,287 --> 01:02:30,788
‎Please stop following me!

1057
01:02:31,622 --> 01:02:33,583
‎You damn bastard!

1058
01:02:38,045 --> 01:02:40,756
‎Hey, let's just talk for a minute!

1059
01:02:40,757 --> 01:02:43,551
‎I've got something important today.
‎Let's talk this out.

1060
01:02:52,518 --> 01:02:54,812
‎Please stop following me!

1061
01:02:55,313 --> 01:02:57,899
‎You damn bastard!

1062
01:03:05,823 --> 01:03:06,699
‎Oh, jeez.

1063
01:03:09,786 --> 01:03:10,870
‎Damn, where'd he go?

1064
01:03:21,130 --> 01:03:22,131
‎This is driving me crazy.

1065
01:03:41,692 --> 01:03:42,568
‎Did I just shoot him?

1066
01:03:44,612 --> 01:03:45,779
‎Excuse me.

1067
01:03:45,780 --> 01:03:48,532
‎You're not dead, are you?
‎Oh god, you can't die.

1068
01:03:48,533 --> 01:03:49,492
‎Hold on.

1069
01:03:51,994 --> 01:03:52,995
‎Wait.

1070
01:03:56,999 --> 01:03:58,416
‎If I get arrested again...

1071
01:03:58,417 --> 01:03:59,793
‎Was this your first time? If not...

1072
01:03:59,794 --> 01:04:02,171
‎You're being accused of exhibitionism.
‎Any comments?

1073
01:04:04,423 --> 01:04:05,383
‎No.

1074
01:04:09,887 --> 01:04:11,179
<i>‎Who's this prick now?</i>

1075
01:04:11,180 --> 01:04:12,682
<i>‎Who's this idiot?</i>

1076
01:04:13,558 --> 01:04:14,851
‎Oh, hello.

1077
01:04:15,518 --> 01:04:16,434
<i>‎Something's fishy.</i>

1078
01:04:16,435 --> 01:04:17,937
‎Yes, hello.

1079
01:04:18,688 --> 01:04:19,772
<i>‎Something's off about him.</i>

1080
01:04:20,690 --> 01:04:23,109
‎Oh, I'm just taking a walk.

1081
01:04:23,901 --> 01:04:25,235
‎Me too.

1082
01:04:25,236 --> 01:04:26,529
<i>‎Taking a walk, here?</i>

1083
01:04:27,655 --> 01:04:28,531
‎Just out for a walk.

1084
01:04:29,824 --> 01:04:30,700
<i>‎Is he out of his mind?</i>

1085
01:04:32,660 --> 01:04:33,703
‎Do I know you

1086
01:04:35,037 --> 01:04:35,954
‎from somewhere?

1087
01:04:35,955 --> 01:04:38,583
‎I do feel like you look familiar.

1088
01:04:40,668 --> 01:04:41,502
‎Have we met before?

1089
01:04:44,005 --> 01:04:45,798
‎-Did you do that?
‎-It wasn't me!

1090
01:04:48,885 --> 01:04:50,887
‎Hey, what are you doing? Push harder.

1091
01:05:01,981 --> 01:05:03,232
‎It won't budge!

1092
01:05:06,819 --> 01:05:08,070
‎This isn't working.

1093
01:05:09,363 --> 01:05:10,239
‎Do-mi.

1094
01:05:10,740 --> 01:05:12,825
‎-I feel dizzy.
‎-You can stop now.

1095
01:05:16,579 --> 01:05:18,371
‎Do-mi, my head feels weird.

1096
01:05:18,372 --> 01:05:19,749
‎What's that clunker?

1097
01:05:24,879 --> 01:05:26,922
<i>‎Hello, Hyun-woo. When are you arriving?</i>

1098
01:05:26,923 --> 01:05:29,549
<i>‎Rehearsal's about to start.
‎The producer's looking for you.</i>

1099
01:05:29,550 --> 01:05:31,134
<i>‎Oh, is he?</i>

1100
01:05:31,135 --> 01:05:33,762
‎Well, we're perfectly prepared,

1101
01:05:33,763 --> 01:05:35,181
‎so we don't need a rehearsal.

1102
01:05:36,390 --> 01:05:37,474
‎You won't be late, right?

1103
01:05:37,475 --> 01:05:40,978
‎-Oh, of course we won't be late.
‎-Hi, Choi Seong-gon here!

1104
01:05:41,729 --> 01:05:43,355
‎I'm with them, and we're running late.

1105
01:05:43,356 --> 01:05:45,775
‎You're with Seong-gon?

1106
01:05:46,359 --> 01:05:48,443
‎Yes, we're on our way together.

1107
01:05:48,444 --> 01:05:50,570
<i>‎Didn't he say you guys are running late?</i>

1108
01:05:50,571 --> 01:05:53,865
‎Hyun-woo, you cannot be late,
‎no matter what.

1109
01:05:53,866 --> 01:05:55,618
‎Sorry, see you soon.

1110
01:05:57,119 --> 01:05:59,580
‎-Hey, what are we going to do with him?
‎-Seriously.

1111
01:06:00,164 --> 01:06:01,498
‎Has he been shot anywhere?

1112
01:06:01,499 --> 01:06:03,124
‎Look closely. I swear he's been shot.

1113
01:06:03,125 --> 01:06:04,626
‎I said I didn't shoot him!

1114
01:06:04,627 --> 01:06:06,544
‎Don't put this all on me.

1115
01:06:06,545 --> 01:06:09,005
‎If you're innocent,
‎the police will clear it up.

1116
01:06:09,006 --> 01:06:10,423
‎Let's go to the police station.

1117
01:06:10,424 --> 01:06:11,675
‎The police?

1118
01:06:11,676 --> 01:06:13,344
‎What do you mean, the police?

1119
01:06:14,887 --> 01:06:17,305
‎How can you say that to an old friend
‎you haven't seen in years?

1120
01:06:17,306 --> 01:06:19,933
‎Friend, my ass.

1121
01:06:19,934 --> 01:06:22,519
‎-You're the reason we disbanded!
‎-That's right.

1122
01:06:22,520 --> 01:06:26,106
‎-Your plagiarism scandal broke you up.
‎-Plagiarism?

1123
01:06:26,107 --> 01:06:28,942
‎The drugs and the plagiarism...
‎The plagiarism scandal did kill us.

1124
01:06:28,943 --> 01:06:31,277
‎-I mean, it's true.
‎-Oh, shit.

1125
01:06:31,278 --> 01:06:32,779
‎What? Did you find a bullet wound?

1126
01:06:32,780 --> 01:06:34,657
‎I just caught his eye.

1127
01:06:35,199 --> 01:06:36,324
‎Oh, he's awake?

1128
01:06:36,325 --> 01:06:37,827
‎Goddammit.

1129
01:06:38,327 --> 01:06:39,996
‎I think he's faking it.

1130
01:06:40,830 --> 01:06:43,540
‎If I catch his eye one more time, I swear...

1131
01:06:43,541 --> 01:06:46,543
<i>‎Seobu Intersection Control,
‎emergency dispatch. Accident reported.</i>

1132
01:06:46,544 --> 01:06:49,421
<i>‎Report of a vehicle collision
‎resulting in a fall.</i>

1133
01:06:49,422 --> 01:06:52,716
<i>‎Location is San 58,
‎Jucheon-ro, Seobu-gu, Gangwon.</i>

1134
01:06:52,717 --> 01:06:54,427
<i>‎Confirm situation on scene and report.</i>

1135
01:06:55,011 --> 01:06:57,596
‎We're arrived at the scene.
‎Vehicle confirmed.

1136
01:06:58,180 --> 01:07:00,141
‎License plate number, 8340...

1137
01:07:02,768 --> 01:07:04,478
‎That's the Mercedes from earlier!

1138
01:07:14,530 --> 01:07:15,865
‎We have a police car behind us.

1139
01:07:26,333 --> 01:07:27,251
‎Hide. Get down!

1140
01:07:42,058 --> 01:07:43,100
‎What is that?

1141
01:07:43,642 --> 01:07:47,687
‎PROFESSIONAL HUNTER
‎WILDLIFE CONTROL SPECIALIST

1142
01:07:47,688 --> 01:07:49,190
‎Is he out of his mind?

1143
01:07:53,778 --> 01:07:55,821
‎Why are you ducking? You need to drive!

1144
01:07:58,199 --> 01:07:59,325
‎Is this a Tesla?

1145
01:08:03,954 --> 01:08:05,790
‎Hey, pull over for a minute.

1146
01:08:09,168 --> 01:08:11,087
‎I said, pull over.

1147
01:08:37,071 --> 01:08:38,364
‎Are you out of your mind?

1148
01:08:44,870 --> 01:08:45,913
‎What's going on here?

1149
01:08:55,422 --> 01:08:56,966
‎Is there something down there?

1150
01:09:01,679 --> 01:09:03,180
‎You're those guys from earlier.

1151
01:09:04,014 --> 01:09:06,474
‎-Oh, hello.
‎-Hello.

1152
01:09:06,475 --> 01:09:09,602
‎We've got a performance today,
‎so we're in a hurry.

1153
01:09:09,603 --> 01:09:10,855
‎We're singers, you see.

1154
01:09:13,315 --> 01:09:14,608
‎Don't you recognize me?

1155
01:09:15,526 --> 01:09:18,612
‎-Allure Queen Byeon Do-mi. Remember?
‎-Peace.

1156
01:09:19,238 --> 01:09:20,447
‎Sure.

1157
01:09:22,533 --> 01:09:23,617
‎Who's this guy here?

1158
01:09:25,911 --> 01:09:27,037
‎I'm a singer too.

1159
01:09:28,455 --> 01:09:29,915
‎Love you.

1160
01:09:52,855 --> 01:09:54,064
‎What's that?

1161
01:09:55,232 --> 01:09:56,317
‎What is?

1162
01:09:59,612 --> 01:10:01,070
‎What is that?

1163
01:10:01,071 --> 01:10:03,281
‎This? It was in the car.

1164
01:10:03,282 --> 01:10:04,200
‎Freeze!

1165
01:10:05,576 --> 01:10:06,951
‎What's happening?

1166
01:10:06,952 --> 01:10:09,788
‎-Drop the gun and put your hands up.
‎-Drop the gun and hands up!

1167
01:10:10,623 --> 01:10:11,456
‎Please, I'm sorry!

1168
01:10:11,457 --> 01:10:13,875
‎-That rifle's his. This guy.
‎-Yes, that's right.

1169
01:10:13,876 --> 01:10:15,669
‎Yes, I'm a hunter.

1170
01:10:16,795 --> 01:10:18,672
‎-Not a singer?
‎-I work as a hunter now.

1171
01:10:21,091 --> 01:10:23,427
‎-Move those clothes aside.
‎-Okay, all right.

1172
01:10:24,678 --> 01:10:26,096
‎-No, no.
‎-No.

1173
01:10:26,889 --> 01:10:28,223
‎What the hell!

1174
01:10:28,224 --> 01:10:29,349
‎You killed that foreigner!

1175
01:10:29,350 --> 01:10:32,394
‎No, he's pretending to be unconscious.
‎He's totally fine.

1176
01:10:34,939 --> 01:10:37,607
‎Hands off the wheel, step out of the car.
‎This is live ammo.

1177
01:10:37,608 --> 01:10:40,485
‎We're getting out.
‎We just need to make it to the stage.

1178
01:10:40,486 --> 01:10:42,987
‎What stage?
‎You're under arrest for murder!

1179
01:10:42,988 --> 01:10:44,031
‎"Arrest"?

1180
01:10:45,699 --> 01:10:47,076
‎I cannot get arrested.

1181
01:10:53,207 --> 01:10:54,040
‎Get them!

1182
01:10:54,041 --> 01:10:55,500
‎What the hell are you doing?

1183
01:10:55,501 --> 01:10:58,337
‎I lost 20 long years of my life.

1184
01:10:59,338 --> 01:11:01,047
‎I can't live like that again.

1185
01:11:01,048 --> 01:11:02,590
‎Snap out of it.

1186
01:11:02,591 --> 01:11:04,550
‎-Do this, and we really can't perform.
‎-Hey.

1187
01:11:04,551 --> 01:11:06,970
‎Are you seriously worried
‎about the performance?

1188
01:11:06,971 --> 01:11:08,055
‎Quiet, everyone.

1189
01:11:09,932 --> 01:11:11,724
‎Yes, Ms. Yang, we're almost there.

1190
01:11:11,725 --> 01:11:13,476
‎Oh, we're now...

1191
01:11:13,477 --> 01:11:14,894
‎We're downtown in Gangwon.

1192
01:11:14,895 --> 01:11:16,562
‎Hey, did you pass out?

1193
01:11:16,563 --> 01:11:19,899
‎Seriously, the producer
‎is furious right now.

1194
01:11:19,900 --> 01:11:21,693
‎Oh, is he?

1195
01:11:21,694 --> 01:11:24,612
‎Hey, Gu Sang-gu! Seriously...

1196
01:11:24,613 --> 01:11:27,241
<i>‎This is a live broadcast.
‎You can't be this late.</i>

1197
01:11:28,659 --> 01:11:31,578
‎If you're late for rehearsal,
‎he'll replace you.

1198
01:11:32,246 --> 01:11:33,997
‎What? There's a backup?

1199
01:11:33,998 --> 01:11:35,915
‎Hey, tell them not to bother coming.

1200
01:11:35,916 --> 01:11:38,459
‎Hey, forget it! Don't come!

1201
01:11:38,460 --> 01:11:40,503
<i>‎Hurry. Get here as soon as you can!</i>

1202
01:11:40,504 --> 01:11:41,922
‎I swear, we won't be late.

1203
01:11:42,840 --> 01:11:43,756
‎We're really close.

1204
01:11:43,757 --> 01:11:46,135
<i>‎-Forget it. Don't come!
‎-Just hurry.</i>

1205
01:11:47,303 --> 01:11:48,137
‎Step on it.

1206
01:11:49,763 --> 01:11:51,597
‎You crazy idiots, just give up already.

1207
01:11:51,598 --> 01:11:53,099
‎Step on it, now!

1208
01:11:53,100 --> 01:11:56,020
‎Let's go!

1209
01:12:04,695 --> 01:12:06,196
‎They've got their siren on!

1210
01:12:10,743 --> 01:12:12,201
‎Are you really going to shoot?

1211
01:12:12,202 --> 01:12:14,495
‎I told you, I saw a dead man in the car.

1212
01:12:14,496 --> 01:12:16,414
‎They're real murderers.

1213
01:12:16,415 --> 01:12:18,541
‎Wee-woo, police car's coming.

1214
01:12:18,542 --> 01:12:20,960
‎-Hey, stop the car.
‎-No.

1215
01:12:20,961 --> 01:12:22,670
‎We don't have time. We have to perform.

1216
01:12:22,671 --> 01:12:24,882
‎We have to catch them. Close in now!

1217
01:12:31,597 --> 01:12:32,973
‎Those crazy bastards.

1218
01:12:45,027 --> 01:12:46,111
‎Pull over!

1219
01:12:49,156 --> 01:12:50,699
‎Pull over!

1220
01:12:52,368 --> 01:12:53,744
‎Hey, watch out!

1221
01:13:00,459 --> 01:13:02,126
‎Are they crazy? We didn't do anything.

1222
01:13:02,127 --> 01:13:04,003
‎You're the craziest one here, damn it!

1223
01:13:04,004 --> 01:13:05,838
‎Hey, we didn't do anything wrong.

1224
01:13:05,839 --> 01:13:08,132
‎It's their own fault
‎for firing recklessly.

1225
01:13:08,133 --> 01:13:10,051
‎You're sure we can perform today, right?

1226
01:13:10,052 --> 01:13:13,513
‎I really need to do my new rap.
‎My mom's been waiting so long for this.

1227
01:13:13,514 --> 01:13:15,014
‎Wait, why did you write a new rap?

1228
01:13:15,015 --> 01:13:18,393
‎You didn't know? I'm filling the intro,
‎interlude, and outro with my rap.

1229
01:13:18,394 --> 01:13:19,852
‎What the hell are you saying?

1230
01:13:19,853 --> 01:13:21,896
‎-No, we'll stick to the original version.
‎-Yeah.

1231
01:13:21,897 --> 01:13:23,023
‎The original version?

1232
01:13:24,608 --> 01:13:25,692
‎So you lied to me?

1233
01:13:26,527 --> 01:13:29,278
‎Let's just get there first, all right?

1234
01:13:29,279 --> 01:13:31,114
‎Next time,
‎you can rap as much as you want.

1235
01:13:31,115 --> 01:13:34,033
‎Next time? So you lied to me.

1236
01:13:34,034 --> 01:13:37,161
‎Let's just focus on the performance
‎and do a good job, okay?

1237
01:13:37,162 --> 01:13:39,080
‎You lied to me, you jerk!

1238
01:13:39,081 --> 01:13:41,250
‎-You bastard! How could you...
‎-Hey.

1239
01:13:41,792 --> 01:13:43,709
‎-Hey!
‎-Is that really important now?

1240
01:13:43,710 --> 01:13:46,838
‎-Let's just get there first, okay?
‎-No!

1241
01:13:46,839 --> 01:13:47,964
‎Son of a bitch!

1242
01:13:47,965 --> 01:13:49,632
‎That's enough!

1243
01:13:49,633 --> 01:13:51,384
‎-Hey, Hwang Hyun-woo!
‎-Come on.

1244
01:13:51,385 --> 01:13:54,595
‎You're supposed to be the leader,
‎but you can't even fix anything!

1245
01:13:54,596 --> 01:13:55,930
‎And you, Gu Sang-gu.

1246
01:13:55,931 --> 01:13:58,975
‎I wouldn't even complain
‎if you were actually a good rapper.

1247
01:13:58,976 --> 01:14:02,979
‎Gosh, what am I even doing
‎with you idiots?

1248
01:14:02,980 --> 01:14:04,773
‎Damn it, I need a smoke.

1249
01:14:06,233 --> 01:14:08,569
‎What about my third album then? Oh, shit.

1250
01:14:12,406 --> 01:14:13,949
‎You've signed for another album?

1251
01:14:14,616 --> 01:14:16,159
‎I need to show them.

1252
01:14:16,160 --> 01:14:18,328
‎Show what? What the hell is your problem?

1253
01:14:18,829 --> 01:14:21,247
‎What kind of lunatic told you
‎to make another album?

1254
01:14:21,248 --> 01:14:23,207
‎Which scumbag producer was it?

1255
01:14:23,208 --> 01:14:24,251
‎My dad.

1256
01:14:25,210 --> 01:14:26,043
‎What?

1257
01:14:26,044 --> 01:14:28,255
‎My dad wanted to help me,

1258
01:14:29,965 --> 01:14:32,217
‎so he took out a loan and sold our house...

1259
01:14:33,051 --> 01:14:34,094
‎Oh, goodness.

1260
01:14:36,138 --> 01:14:38,599
‎-Just to help this useless son...
‎-Oh, boy.

1261
01:14:40,184 --> 01:14:41,894
‎It's all my fault.

1262
01:14:42,436 --> 01:14:44,270
‎-What's going on?
‎-Huh?

1263
01:14:44,271 --> 01:14:45,272
‎What's wrong with the car?

1264
01:14:46,273 --> 01:14:48,192
‎-Hey!
‎-Stop!

1265
01:14:49,943 --> 01:14:50,860
‎Hey, stop!

1266
01:14:50,861 --> 01:14:53,113
‎Stop!

1267
01:14:57,451 --> 01:14:58,285
<i>‎Dad!</i>

1268
01:15:13,509 --> 01:15:15,510
‎Yes, Ms. Yang. We're almost there.

1269
01:15:15,511 --> 01:15:16,677
‎-We'll--
‎-<i>‎Are you insane?</i>

1270
01:15:16,678 --> 01:15:18,721
‎How can you be late
‎to a live show I'm directing?

1271
01:15:18,722 --> 01:15:20,932
‎You're never working with me again.
‎Got it?

1272
01:15:20,933 --> 01:15:23,684
‎No, sir, please...

1273
01:15:23,685 --> 01:15:24,603
<i>‎I'm hanging up!</i>

1274
01:15:37,699 --> 01:15:39,825
‎Hey, where's the backup?

1275
01:15:39,826 --> 01:15:41,285
‎They're on their way.

1276
01:15:41,286 --> 01:15:42,704
‎Who? Someone famous?

1277
01:15:44,331 --> 01:15:45,874
‎There they are.

1278
01:15:46,542 --> 01:15:47,917
‎You know them, right?

1279
01:15:47,918 --> 01:15:49,253
‎Kong Kong Girls.

1280
01:15:52,297 --> 01:15:54,590
‎Tell them to just turn around and leave.

1281
01:15:54,591 --> 01:15:57,260
‎-Yes, you can go.
‎-I'm sorry. Please go.

1282
01:15:57,261 --> 01:15:59,680
‎Can't you get off those things and walk?

1283
01:16:02,099 --> 01:16:03,182
‎-Sir.
‎-That's too much.

1284
01:16:03,183 --> 01:16:04,976
‎Na Tae-poong's in Sancheok now.

1285
01:16:04,977 --> 01:16:07,436
‎If he leaves now,
‎he'll make it in time for our finale.

1286
01:16:07,437 --> 01:16:08,479
‎-Na Tae-poong?
‎-Yes.

1287
01:16:08,480 --> 01:16:11,399
‎-Tell him to come now. Hurry!
‎-Okay, got it.

1288
01:16:11,400 --> 01:16:13,652
‎It's all over now.

1289
01:16:14,778 --> 01:16:16,613
‎I've lost my last chance at a comeback.

1290
01:16:18,782 --> 01:16:20,200
‎It's over now.

1291
01:16:21,952 --> 01:16:25,538
‎They say
‎everyone gets three chances in life.

1292
01:16:25,539 --> 01:16:27,207
‎They're wrong.

1293
01:16:27,833 --> 01:16:30,960
‎Who's generous enough
‎to give you three chances?

1294
01:16:30,961 --> 01:16:32,921
‎You should've seized it
‎when it first came.

1295
01:16:33,505 --> 01:16:35,256
<i>‎I knew this would happen</i>

1296
01:16:35,257 --> 01:16:38,135
<i>‎I shouldn't have gotten my hopes up</i>

1297
01:16:38,802 --> 01:16:41,847
<i>‎I knew we were going to fail anyway</i>

1298
01:16:42,639 --> 01:16:44,849
<i>‎My shattered beat</i>

1299
01:16:44,850 --> 01:16:47,769
<i>‎The rhyming verse
‎I'll be spitting as I die</i>

1300
01:16:49,104 --> 01:16:51,856
‎Are you okay? Snap out of it, man!

1301
01:16:51,857 --> 01:16:52,899
<i>‎Snap out of it?</i>

1302
01:16:54,484 --> 01:16:56,944
<i>‎You snap out of it, bang, bang</i>

1303
01:16:56,945 --> 01:16:59,739
<i>‎Your singing sucks just as much as my rap</i>

1304
01:16:59,740 --> 01:17:03,326
‎Hey, your rap sucks big-time.
‎You call that a rhyme?

1305
01:17:03,327 --> 01:17:05,202
<i>‎Freestyle is all the same</i>

1306
01:17:05,203 --> 01:17:07,872
<i>‎If that's freestyle, I could do it too</i>

1307
01:17:07,873 --> 01:17:10,459
<i>‎You just have to match the last syllable
‎That's it</i>

1308
01:17:11,835 --> 01:17:14,503
<i>‎Maybe I could be a rapper too</i>

1309
01:17:14,504 --> 01:17:16,422
<i>‎And quit being a ballad singer</i>

1310
01:17:16,423 --> 01:17:18,842
<i>‎I think I'm pretty good
‎Love you</i>

1311
01:17:19,426 --> 01:17:20,885
‎Screw off, weirdo.

1312
01:17:20,886 --> 01:17:23,804
<i>‎Oh, I can freestyle rap
‎Freestyle</i>

1313
01:17:23,805 --> 01:17:25,640
<i>‎You're doing it freestyle
‎I can do it too</i>

1314
01:17:25,641 --> 01:17:29,061
<i>‎I'm just winging it, winging it
‎And it turns into rap, yo</i>

1315
01:17:29,645 --> 01:17:31,480
‎You're nowhere near my level.

1316
01:17:32,230 --> 01:17:34,023
‎I'm offended, so cut it out.

1317
01:17:34,024 --> 01:17:35,066
<i>‎Yo</i>

1318
01:17:35,067 --> 01:17:38,069
<i>‎Whose fault is it
‎That we're in this mess now, yo</i>

1319
01:17:38,070 --> 01:17:40,988
<i>‎Why is our leader keeping his mouth shut?</i>

1320
01:17:40,989 --> 01:17:41,948
<i>‎Pass!</i>

1321
01:17:44,576 --> 01:17:45,494
‎Hey, leader!

1322
01:17:46,995 --> 01:17:49,456
‎Say something. What now?

1323
01:18:17,651 --> 01:18:19,695
‎Hey, what's with you?

1324
01:18:23,240 --> 01:18:25,242
‎I think they hit their heads in the crash.

1325
01:18:27,494 --> 01:18:28,787
‎They've both lost their minds.

1326
01:18:42,134 --> 01:18:42,968
‎Yes, Ms. Yang.

1327
01:18:43,719 --> 01:18:45,344
‎We're really almost there.

1328
01:18:45,345 --> 01:18:47,221
‎-<i>‎Really?</i>
‎-We're outside the venue.

1329
01:18:47,222 --> 01:18:49,640
<i>‎If you're not here, we're replacing you.</i>

1330
01:18:49,641 --> 01:18:52,436
‎Yes, see you in a bit.

1331
01:18:58,775 --> 01:19:01,110
‎You only get three chances in life?

1332
01:19:01,111 --> 01:19:03,822
‎That's way too few. That's not fair.

1333
01:19:04,531 --> 01:19:06,742
‎It's only natural
‎to fail three times in life.

1334
01:19:08,368 --> 01:19:09,870
‎Shouldn't we get dozens of chances?

1335
01:19:10,454 --> 01:19:11,538
‎Don't you agree?

1336
01:19:12,998 --> 01:19:16,000
‎Even if war breaks out or aliens attack,

1337
01:19:16,001 --> 01:19:17,793
‎we're taking the stage today!

1338
01:19:17,794 --> 01:19:19,421
‎You got that, Byeon Do-mi?

1339
01:19:20,714 --> 01:19:21,547
‎What?

1340
01:19:21,548 --> 01:19:23,925
‎You left the house for once.
‎You need to get on stage!

1341
01:19:24,676 --> 01:19:27,011
‎-Hell yeah.
‎-And you, Gu Sang-gu.

1342
01:19:27,012 --> 01:19:28,929
‎You can't let that new rap go to waste!

1343
01:19:28,930 --> 01:19:30,681
‎No way, I have to do it. Let's go!

1344
01:19:30,682 --> 01:19:33,768
‎Why are you all quiet, you little shit?
‎Don't you want to perform?

1345
01:19:33,769 --> 01:19:35,978
‎I want to, you little shit!

1346
01:19:35,979 --> 01:19:37,063
‎But we don't have a car.

1347
01:19:38,023 --> 01:19:39,983
‎What's that? Is that a boat?

1348
01:19:40,567 --> 01:19:42,319
‎There's a car passing by every minute!

1349
01:19:43,904 --> 01:19:46,531
‎We've got no time and nothing to lose.
‎Get your stuff!

1350
01:19:47,699 --> 01:19:50,201
‎We've got nothing to lose...

1351
01:19:50,202 --> 01:19:52,496
‎Wait, this is yours.

1352
01:19:53,789 --> 01:19:56,999
‎My gosh. Hey, this is wrong.

1353
01:19:57,000 --> 01:19:57,917
‎Hyun-woo.

1354
01:19:57,918 --> 01:20:00,754
‎I know we all want to perform,
‎but we can't commit a crime!

1355
01:20:02,130 --> 01:20:03,840
‎Don't you know what hitchhiking is?

1356
01:20:04,466 --> 01:20:05,634
‎Don't you know?

1357
01:20:10,263 --> 01:20:11,598
‎-Here.
‎-Jeez.

1358
01:20:13,225 --> 01:20:14,726
‎What do we do with him?

1359
01:20:15,310 --> 01:20:17,812
‎I swear, I caught his eye earlier.

1360
01:20:17,813 --> 01:20:20,148
‎He's just pretending to be passed out.

1361
01:20:21,733 --> 01:20:23,860
‎But why's he still keeping up the act?

1362
01:20:25,195 --> 01:20:26,028
‎Mr. Park.

1363
01:20:26,029 --> 01:20:29,574
‎If you're doing this
‎because you know you owe us money,

1364
01:20:30,158 --> 01:20:32,285
‎let's just call it even now.

1365
01:20:37,207 --> 01:20:39,250
‎What can we do about it now anyway?

1366
01:20:39,251 --> 01:20:41,877
‎Want me to put it in writing
‎that we'll let bygones be bygones?

1367
01:20:41,878 --> 01:20:43,420
‎-Yes, do that!
‎-What the...

1368
01:20:43,421 --> 01:20:45,130
‎-Oh, shit!
‎-I told you!

1369
01:20:45,131 --> 01:20:47,299
‎-Jeez.
‎-Oh, boy.

1370
01:20:47,300 --> 01:20:49,177
‎What happened to my neck?

1371
01:20:49,761 --> 01:20:50,594
‎Listen, guys.

1372
01:20:50,595 --> 01:20:53,055
‎Old-school K-pop is taking off again
‎in South America.

1373
01:20:53,056 --> 01:20:55,851
‎I'll pick a few groups
‎and break them into that market.

1374
01:20:56,434 --> 01:20:58,186
‎Why didn't I know
‎you were performing today?

1375
01:20:58,770 --> 01:21:00,146
‎You haven't changed at all.

1376
01:21:01,147 --> 01:21:02,148
‎Let's go hit the stage.

1377
01:21:03,233 --> 01:21:04,067
‎Let's go.

1378
01:21:06,528 --> 01:21:08,572
‎Here, please!

1379
01:21:09,155 --> 01:21:11,157
‎Love you!

1380
01:21:16,121 --> 01:21:17,788
‎Put your hands in the air!

1381
01:21:17,789 --> 01:21:20,166
‎-You're under arrest for murder.
‎-Freeze!

1382
01:21:21,167 --> 01:21:22,502
‎Who died?

1383
01:21:23,128 --> 01:21:24,753
‎Don't you understand Korean?

1384
01:21:24,754 --> 01:21:27,631
‎I crashed my car
